  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1002 AM CST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nThis coming Thanksgiving continues to exhibit below- average \ntemperatures through next weekend. Overall, synoptic models \nremain in good agreement with a progression of upper level waves\nhelping to reinforce the cold weather and the upper level flow\nbecoming northwesterly by Friday. This will act to allow the \ncold polar airmass to remain over the region. NBM percentile \ndata keep relatively tight temperature spreads for daily highs \nand lows through the week with only spreads of 2 to 4 degrees. \nSpread increase a bit into next weekend, but that is 7 days out \nand expected. \n\nDaily highs are not forecast to reach 50 degrees until after\nThanksgiving Day, with overnight lows into the 20s.\n\nModels and ensembles are still hinting at a slight chance for\nanother shot of precipitation by Friday, but the hint is more of\na wink and a nod with precipitation potential less than 20% \nthrough the long term period.",
